# Sensitive configurations & Credentials
.env
.env.*
.env-*
!.env.example
.git-credentials
*token*
*credential*
credentials.json
client_secret*.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# Neither is where a real credential lives -- `~/.drunken/secrets.json` is
# outside any checkout, and the .bak files this project writes land beside the
# host config they back up. Both are where one gets copied to "just for a
# minute", which is the same story `.env` above already has a rule for (DG-325).
*.bak
secrets.json

# Local agent state and logs -- the Discord daemon writes its logs here, and
# other agents' runtimes may too. None of it is tracked. The two files once
# carved out of this rule (`.agents/AGENTS.md`, `.agents/hooks.json`) were
# Antigravity's and are retired (DG-349). Skills and agents have one source, in
# `skills/` and `agents/`, and scripts/check_ignored_sources.py stops a rule
# like this from swallowing a real source file unnoticed (DG-259).
.agents/

# Local Claude Code state (worktrees, scheduled tasks, checkpoints, etc.).
# settings.json is the one exception: it is the shared permission allowlist
# and denylist, so it has to ship with the repo -- a tool other people can
# use safely is the whole point (Boss's rule 4). Personal overrides belong in
# settings.local.json, which stays ignored.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json

# Local scratch. Dockerfile used to be listed here as "simulation config, do
# not commit" -- DG-228 made it a deliverable (it is how the pinned install is
# verified), and the stale rule silently kept it out of #114 while the PR
# described it in detail. Found by DG-259's own test failing in CI.
scratch_*.py

# DG-314. The rule above is a filename prefix and was read for years as if it
# covered this directory too. It never did: `scratch/claude_advice.txt` and
# `scratch/claude_response.txt`, both zero bytes, reached develop in PR #48 --
# the PR that was meant to carry the checkpoint and carried only these.
# check_ignored_sources.py was right to stay quiet; `scratch` is not one of its
# SOURCE_DIRS, so nothing under it is ever source to that guard. The gap was
# here, not there.
scratch/
not_use/

# Generated by `drunken-config --kind install` from uv.lock. Regenerable,
# and committing it would put a second source of truth beside the lock.
requirements.lock.txt

# Retired code. Kept on disk, deliberately not committed -- DG-291.
# `an agent does not delete` exists so work is not lost; it is not a rule to
# publish. This directory was tracked only because nothing here excluded it, and
# publishing it shipped a drifted duplicate of a live skill, drew Dependabot
# alerts and a merged pull request against withdrawn code, and stood as a second
# archive beside git history. The index that stays committed is RETIRED.md.
_not_used/

# Session scratchpad for cross-agent coordination -- not project record.
# The Boss confirmed this is working state, not history: it belongs to
# whoever's session wrote it, not to git. Anchored to root so it does not
# swallow templates/SESSION_CHECKPOINT.md, the tracked template this file is
# generated from.
/SESSION_CHECKPOINT.md

# DG-313 / DG-250: operating config, not source. It names this machine
# paths and which project each server serves, so it lives at the wrapper
# level and is generated by scripts/install/install_mcp.sh.
.mcp.json
